# Product and Engineering Specification

## Goal

Deliver a native Rust Qwen3-TTS 12 Hz runtime whose model behavior and deployment surfaces are
equivalent to qwentts.cpp for supported model families while retaining Rust-native APIs.

## Supported Model Matrix

Required:

- Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-Base
- Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-0.6B-CustomVoice
- Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-Base
- Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-CustomVoice
- Qwen3-TTS-12Hz-1.7B-VoiceDesign
- shared Qwen3-TTS-Tokenizer-12Hz encoder and decoder

## Functional Requirements

### TTS Generation

- Text input, language selection and automatic language mode.
- Base default synthesis.
- x-vector-only voice clone.
- ICL voice clone with reference audio and transcript.
- CustomVoice named speakers and dialect metadata.
- VoiceDesign free-text instructions.
- Separate Talker and Code Predictor sampling options.
- deterministic seed behavior.

### Streaming

- Audio callback/chunk must occur before full token generation completes.
- Every generated codec frame is immediately eligible for codec decode.
- One frame produces 1920 samples at 24 kHz.
- Persistent state must include convolution context, transposed-convolution overlap,
  transformer KV window, absolute position and output bookkeeping.
- Reset must reproduce clean offline zero-padding behavior.
- Multiple sessions must have isolated states.

### Tokenizer

- Encode 24 kHz mono WAV into 16 RVQ codes at 12.5 Hz.
- Decode codes into 24 kHz mono PCM.
- Buffered chunk decode and true stateful stream decode.
- Round-trip file format with version and model metadata.

### Model Storage and Quantization

- Metadata must be read from model/config files; no model-family behavior derived only from names.
- Support F32/BF16 baseline.
- Support native Q8_0 and Q4_K_M-class inference for eligible Talker tensors.
- Sensitive RVQ codebooks, projections, speaker encoder and small/nonnormal tensors remain F32/F16
  according to a documented policy.
- Runtime must not materialize a full F32 copy of quantized backbone weights.

### Product Surfaces

- `qwen-tts`: text to WAV or streamed PCM.
- `qwen-codec`: WAV to codes and codes to WAV.
- `tts-server`: OpenAI-compatible `/v1/audio/speech`; streaming response.
- Rust library API.
- C ABI shared library.
- Optional existing egui GUI remains supported.

## Non-Functional Requirements

- No O(n²) history recomputation in streaming.
- Bounded per-session memory.
- Cancellation is checked between generation/decode frames.
- No global mutable session state.
- Errors include phase and model context.
- CPU correctness is the numerical reference.
- CUDA and Metal use backend-specific performance gates.
- Large models and fixtures are external assets with checksums.

## Exclusions

- 25 Hz Flow Matching decoder is not required for qwentts.cpp 12 Hz parity.
- Training and fine-tuning are not part of this package.
- Voice dataset management is out of scope.
